## 5. Kernel orientation (read from `src/`, line-grounded — for a new reader)

**Reduction core, `src/net.c`.** One step is `interact(o, v)` (≈1806): an active pair is always one
operation meeting the single value it consumes — `redex` (≈314) drops any pair of two values or two
operations as a wire nobody reads, and `l->steps++` ticks once per interact, so step count is a
property of the term. Three universal rules fire before any type-specific rule: `O_ERA` erase,
`O_DUP` duplicate (lazy, one level — the O(1) share; a `V_REF` box read is a refcount bump +
one-level copy, ≈1879), `O_SUBST` dimension-substitution. Laziness is the default: `O_FWD` is a parked
read and "not a step" (≈1808); `unbuilt(v)` subterms build on demand (≈1875); a used definition
`V_GLOBAL` copies its body in lazily and parks if not ready (≈1866). Open terms reduce because an
eliminator meeting an unknown `V_UNK` erases its branches and passes the neutral through (≈1886).
Parallelism without locks (`link`/`publish`, ≈334–376): two principals rendezvous through a variable
cell by atomic exchange (`vxchg`, first arrival wins); every wire and made-pair of a rewrite is
deferred and published only when the whole rewrite completes, so no thread sees a half-written cell;
work-stealing deques carry the pairs, neighbours from one rewrite staying on a core.

**Content-addressed store, `src/store.c`.** A checked definition's key is `SHA-256` of the canonical
type+term: binders nameless (`@k`, de Bruijn distance), every dependency replaced by its own key
(`G<key>`/`D<key>`, constructors/fields `C<key>.i`/`F<key>.i`), binder multiplicities kept, and
names/files/positions excluded (`key_def`, ≈618) — so one definition has one key on every machine.
`.cubical-store/<key>/check` is a per-checker certificate (`ok <steps> <checker>`), the checker named
by the hash of the library text loaded up to `%%chk-def` plus the machine binary; a definition with
an `ok` line by the current checker is not rechecked. `names` is an append-only `name key time` log.

