A true subscribe/stream is **not reachable from a cloud agent workspace**: the shell is network-blocked
to the host (`403 … no rule or network setting allows this host` from the agent proxy, both `/` and
`/api/p2p/signal`), so no heartbeat POST, no WebSocket, no WebRTC handshake. Only one-shot page GETs
reach the host, and those cache 15 min. To join the mesh from an agent, allowlist `hyperactivity.ai`
for the workspace shell (network settings) — effective in a new session; then the dispatch's
`./hx agent inbox` / signal-POST flow works.

